.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-moderation 1  "taurctl-moderation " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-moderation \- Reject a package or user, or review those decisions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl moderation\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reject a package or user, or review those decisions
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taurctl\-moderation\-reject\-package(1)
Reject a package base. Moderator or site admin
.TP
taurctl\-moderation\-reject\-user(1)
Reject an ordinary account. Moderator or site admin
.TP
taurctl\-moderation\-audit(1)
List the rejection audit. Site admin
.TP
taurctl\-moderation\-reverse(1)
Reverse one open package or user rejection. Site admin
.TP
taurctl\-moderation\-set\-moderator(1)
Grant or remove the moderator role. Site admin
.TP
taurctl\-moderation\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
